  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given three arrays AAA, BBB, and CCC, all of length NNN. You also have two integers k1k_1k1​ and k2k_2k2​.\n\nFor every index 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N, you must choose **exactly one** of Ai,BiA_i, B_iAi​,Bi​, or CiC_iCi​. Find the **maximum** possible sum of chosen elements, such that:\n\n\nAt most k1k_1k1​ elements are picked from AAA, and\nAt most k2k_2k2​ elements are picked from BBB\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. TTT test cases follow.\nEach test case consists of five lines of input.\nThe first line of each test case contains the integer NNN — the length of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\nThe fourth line contains NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​.\nThe fifth line contains two space-separated integers k1k_1k1​ and k2k_2k2​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum sum possible by selecting the elements under the specified constraints.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\le N \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi,Ci≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i, C_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​,Ci​≤109",
      "0≤k1,k2≤N0 \\le k_1, k_2 \\le N0≤k1​,k2​≤N",
      "It is guaranteed that the sum of NNN across all test cases doesn't exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
